WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.610
Let's jump in to talk about

2
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.105
the self-attention
mechanism of transformers.

3
00:00:09.105 --> 00:00:12.030
If you can get the main
idea behind this video,

4
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.705
you'll understand the
most important core idea

5
00:00:15.705 --> 00:00:17.790
behind what makes
transformer networks

6
00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.440
work. Let's jump in.

7
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.410
You've seen how
attention is used with

8
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.140
sequential neural
networks such as RNNs.

9
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.295
To use attention with a
style more late CNNs,

10
00:00:28.295 --> 00:00:30.890
you need to calculate
self-attention,

11
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:33.860
where you create
attention-based representations

12
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.625
for each of the words
in your input sentence.

13
00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:39.254
Let's use our running example,

14
00:00:39.254 --> 00:00:41.980
Jane, visite, l'Afrique,
en, septembre,

15
00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:45.590
our goal will be for each word to

16
00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:51.745
compute an attention-based
representation like this.

17
00:00:51.745 --> 00:00:55.295
So we'll end up
with five of these,

18
00:00:55.295 --> 00:00:58.070
since our sentence
has five words.

19
00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:00.020
When we've computed them we'll

20
00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.150
call the five
representations with

21
00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:07.365
these five words A1through A5.

22
00:01:07.365 --> 00:01:09.740
I know you're starting
to see a bunch

23
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.250
of symbols Q, K, and V,

24
00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.035
we'll explain what
these symbols mean

25
00:01:15.035 --> 00:01:17.905
in a later slide so don't
worry about them for now.

26
00:01:17.905 --> 00:01:20.525
The running example
I'm going to use

27
00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:24.890
is take the word l'Afrique
in this sentence.

28
00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:27.830
We'll step through on
the next slide how

29
00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.519
the transformer network's
self-attention mechanism

30
00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:36.590
allows you to compute
A3 for this word,

31
00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.000
and then you do
the same thing for

32
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.965
the other words in
the sentence as well.

33
00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:43.150
Now you learn previously
about word embeddings.

34
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.870
One way to represent
l'Afrique would be to just

35
00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.005
look up the word
embedding for l'Afrique.

36
00:01:49.005 --> 00:01:51.830
But depending on the context,

37
00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.940
are we thinking of l'Afrique
or Africa as a site of

38
00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:00.710
historical interests or
as a holiday destination,

39
00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:04.325
or as the world's second
largest continent.

40
00:02:04.325 --> 00:02:07.160
Depending on how you're
thinking of l'Afrique,

41
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.720
you may choose to
represent it differently,

42
00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.940
and that's what this
representation A(3) will do.

43
00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.340
It will look at the
surrounding words

44
00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.080
to try to figure out what's

45
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.180
actually going on in how

46
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.610
we're talking about
Africa in this sentence,

47
00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:26.480
and find the most appropriate
representation for this.

48
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.225
In terms of the
actual calculation,

49
00:02:29.225 --> 00:02:31.510
it won't be too different from

50
00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:33.470
the attention mechanism you saw

51
00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.455
previously as applied
in the context of RNNs,

52
00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:39.140
except we'll compute
these representations

53
00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:42.190
in parallel for all five
words in a sentence.

54
00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:45.620
When we're building
attention on top of RNNs,

55
00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.230
this was the equation we used.

56
00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:50.885
With the self-attention
mechanism,

57
00:02:50.885 --> 00:02:53.060
the attention equation is

58
00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.495
instead going to look like this.

59
00:02:55.495 --> 00:02:59.015
You can see the equations
have some similarity.

60
00:02:59.015 --> 00:03:03.710
The inner term here also
involves a softmax,

61
00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:06.470
just like this term
over here on the left,

62
00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.730
and you can think of

63
00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:14.280
the exponent terms as being
akin to attention values.

64
00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.650
Exactly how these
terms are worked

65
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.065
out you'll see in the next slide.

66
00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:22.210
So again, don't worry about
the details just yet.

67
00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.380
But the main
difference is that for

68
00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.349
every word, say for l'Afrique,

69
00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:36.090
you have three values called
the query, key, and value.

70
00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.740
These vectors are
the key inputs to

71
00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:45.005
computing the attention
value for each words.

72
00:03:45.005 --> 00:03:48.020
Now, let's step through the steps

73
00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:52.225
needed to actually calculate A3.

74
00:03:52.225 --> 00:03:54.240
On this slide, let's step through

75
00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.270
the computations you need
to go from the words

76
00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:02.250
l'Afrique to the self-attention
representation A3.

77
00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.820
For reference, I've
also printed up here on

78
00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.085
the upper-right that softmax-like

79
00:04:07.085 --> 00:04:09.060
equation from the previous slide.

80
00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.385
First, we're going to associate
each of the words with

81
00:04:13.385 --> 00:04:18.365
three values called the
query key and value pairs.

82
00:04:18.365 --> 00:04:24.525
If X3 is the word
embedding for l'Afrique,

83
00:04:24.525 --> 00:04:32.165
the way that's Q3 is computed
is as a learned matrix,

84
00:04:32.165 --> 00:04:38.790
which I'm going to
write as WQ times X3,

85
00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:41.510
and similarly for the
key and value pairs,

86
00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:47.659
so K3 is WK times

87
00:04:47.659 --> 00:04:56.880
X3 and V3 is WV times X3.

88
00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:01.510
These matrices, WQ, WK, and WV,

89
00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:04.710
are parameters of this
learning algorithm,

90
00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.140
and they allow you to
pull off these query,

91
00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:10.745
key, and value vectors
for each word.

92
00:05:10.745 --> 00:05:12.590
So what are these query key

93
00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.495
and value vectors supposed to do?

94
00:05:14.495 --> 00:05:17.450
They were named using a loose
analogy to a concept in

95
00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.670
databases where you can have

96
00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.640
queries and also key-value pairs.

97
00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:25.340
If you're familiar with
those types of databases,

98
00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:27.035
the analogy may
make sense to you,

99
00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:28.160
but if you're not familiar with

100
00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.220
that database concept,
don't worry about it.

101
00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.770
Let me give one intuition

102
00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.500
behind the intent of these query,

103
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.355
key, and value of vectors.

104
00:05:39.355 --> 00:05:45.485
Q3 is a question that you
get to ask about l'Afrique.

105
00:05:45.485 --> 00:05:51.690
Q3 may represent a question
like, what's happening there?

106
00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:55.765
Africa, l'Afrique
is a destination.

107
00:05:55.765 --> 00:05:57.700
You might want to know when

108
00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:01.420
computing A^3, what's
happening there.

109
00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:05.125
What we're going to do is compute

110
00:06:05.125 --> 00:06:09.640
the inner product
between q^3 and k^1,

111
00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.100
between Query 3 and Key 1,

112
00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.654
and this will tell us
how good is an answer

113
00:06:15.654 --> 00:06:17.260
where it's one to

114
00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:19.885
the question of what's
happening in Africa.

115
00:06:19.885 --> 00:06:22.960
Then we compute the
inner product between

116
00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.200
q^3 and k^2 and this
is intended to tell

117
00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:31.360
us how good is visite an
answer to the question of

118
00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.820
what's happening in Africa and so

119
00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:36.955
on for the other words
in the sequence.

120
00:06:36.955 --> 00:06:39.670
The goal of this operation is to

121
00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.595
pull up the most
information that's needed

122
00:06:42.595 --> 00:06:44.500
to help us compute

123
00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:49.370
the most useful
representation A^3 up here.

124
00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:52.735
Again, just for
intuition building

125
00:06:52.735 --> 00:06:57.055
if k^1 represents that
this word is a person,

126
00:06:57.055 --> 00:06:58.570
because Jane is a person,

127
00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:01.975
and k^2 represents
that the second word,

128
00:07:01.975 --> 00:07:04.315
visite, is an action,

129
00:07:04.315 --> 00:07:07.090
then you may find that
q^3 inter producted

130
00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:10.330
with k^2 has the largest value,

131
00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:13.135
and this may be
intuitive example,

132
00:07:13.135 --> 00:07:15.399
might suggest that visite,

133
00:07:15.399 --> 00:07:17.200
gives you the most
relevant contexts

134
00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.625
for what's happening in Africa.

135
00:07:18.625 --> 00:07:22.855
Which is that, it's viewed as
a destination for a visit.

136
00:07:22.855 --> 00:07:25.960
What we will do is take

137
00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.390
these five values in

138
00:07:28.390 --> 00:07:32.245
this row and compute
a Softmax over them.

139
00:07:32.245 --> 00:07:36.250
There's actually this
Softmax over here,

140
00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:39.820
and in the example that
we've been talking about,

141
00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.910
q^3 times k^2 corresponding

142
00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:46.090
to word visite maybe
has the largest value.

143
00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:48.535
I'm going to shade
that blue over here.

144
00:07:48.535 --> 00:07:50.590
Then finally, we're going to take

145
00:07:50.590 --> 00:07:54.895
these Softmax values and
multiply them with v^1,

146
00:07:54.895 --> 00:07:56.920
which is the value for word 1,

147
00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:00.160
the value for word 2, and so on,

148
00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:08.365
and so these values correspond
to that value up there.

149
00:08:08.365 --> 00:08:11.140
Finally, we sum it all up.

150
00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:13.765
This summation corresponds to

151
00:08:13.765 --> 00:08:16.945
this summation operator
and so adding up

152
00:08:16.945 --> 00:08:20.815
all of these values
gives you A^3,

153
00:08:20.815 --> 00:08:23.890
which is just equal
to this value here.

154
00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:28.300
Another way to write
A^3 is really as A,

155
00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:33.385
this A up here of q^3,

156
00:08:33.385 --> 00:08:36.880
k, v. But sometimes it will be

157
00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:40.970
more convenient to just
write A^3 like that.

158
00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:45.520
The key advantage of
this representation is

159
00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:50.335
the word of l'Afrique isn't
some fixed word embedding.

160
00:08:50.335 --> 00:08:54.219
Instead, it lets the
self-attention mechanism

161
00:08:54.219 --> 00:08:58.540
realize that l'Afrique is
the destination of a visite,

162
00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:01.705
of a visit, and thus
compute a richer,

163
00:09:01.705 --> 00:09:05.305
more useful representation
for this word.

164
00:09:05.305 --> 00:09:07.720
Now, I've been using
the third word,

165
00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.940
l'Afrique as a running example

166
00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.670
but you could use this
process for all five

167
00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.860
words in your sequence to get

168
00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.665
similarly rich
representations for Jane,

169
00:09:17.665 --> 00:09:22.285
visite, l'Afrique, en, septembre.

170
00:09:22.285 --> 00:09:27.310
If you put all of these
five computations together,

171
00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:32.125
denotation used in
literature looks like this,

172
00:09:32.125 --> 00:09:33.910
where you can summarize all

173
00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:35.590
of these computations
that we just talked

174
00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.820
about for all the words in

175
00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:39.850
the sequence by
writing Attention(Q,

176
00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:42.280
K, V) where Q, K,

177
00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:46.165
V matrices with all
of these values,

178
00:09:46.165 --> 00:09:47.845
and this is just

179
00:09:47.845 --> 00:09:51.580
a compressed or
vectorized representation

180
00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:54.445
of this equation up here.

181
00:09:54.445 --> 00:09:57.100
The term in the denominator

182
00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:59.019
is just to scale the dot-product,

183
00:09:59.019 --> 00:10:00.385
so it doesn't explode.

184
00:10:00.385 --> 00:10:02.620
You don't really need
to worry about it.

185
00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.620
But another name for
this type of attention

186
00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:09.055
is the scaled
dot-product attention.

187
00:10:09.055 --> 00:10:11.290
This is the one represented in

188
00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.915
the original transformer
architecture paper,

189
00:10:13.915 --> 00:10:16.615
Attention Is All
You Need As Well.

190
00:10:16.615 --> 00:10:19.600
That's the
self-attention mechanism

191
00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.460
of the transformer network.

192
00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:24.070
To recap, associated with each of

193
00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:27.954
the five words you
end up with a query,

194
00:10:27.954 --> 00:10:29.935
a key, and a value.

195
00:10:29.935 --> 00:10:33.175
The query lets you ask a
question about that word,

196
00:10:33.175 --> 00:10:35.350
such as what's
happening in Africa.

197
00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:38.515
The key looks at all
of the other words,

198
00:10:38.515 --> 00:10:41.065
and by the similarity
to the query,

199
00:10:41.065 --> 00:10:43.510
helps you figure out
which words gives

200
00:10:43.510 --> 00:10:46.480
the most relevant answer
to that question.

201
00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.610
In this case, visite is what's

202
00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:51.655
happening in Africa,
someone's visiting Africa.

203
00:10:51.655 --> 00:10:56.080
Then finally, the value
allows the representation to

204
00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:00.700
plug in how visite should
be represented within A^3,

205
00:11:00.700 --> 00:11:03.730
within the representation
of Africa.

206
00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:05.500
This allows you to come up with

207
00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:06.910
a representation for the word

208
00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:09.040
Africa that says this is

209
00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.890
Africa and someone
is visiting Africa.

210
00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:13.480
This is a much more nuanced,

211
00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:16.120
much richer representation
for the world than if you

212
00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.670
just had to pull up the
same fixed word embedding

213
00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:19.810
for every single word

214
00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:22.030
without being able
to adapt it based

215
00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:23.800
on what words are to

216
00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.615
the left and to the
right of that word.

217
00:11:25.615 --> 00:11:28.990
We've all got to take into
account and in the context.

218
00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:33.295
Now, you have learned about
the self-attention mechanism.

219
00:11:33.295 --> 00:11:34.990
We're going to put
a big for-loop

220
00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.490
over this whole thing and that

221
00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:39.670
will be the multi-headed
attention mechanism.

222
00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.520
Let's dive into the details
of that in the next video.